  "design_note": "A calendar-date washout is invalid in MIMIC-IV: dates are shifted into the future by a random per-patient offset, so index intime spans 2110-2210 for care delivered 2011-2019 and cross-patient calendar comparisons are meaningless. Because within-patient intervals are preserved, the lookback is defined per patient as (index visit intime) - (that patient's earliest ED intime in the full edstays table). Patients whose index visit is their first recorded ED encounter have lookback_days = 0. Restricting to a lookback confirms incident status only among patients with prior ED contact in this system, and therefore selects toward prior ED users.",
